        "paragraphs": [
            "Openrouter Auto is a model family from the developer Openrouter. According to Openrouter, the Auto Router automatically selects the best model for your prompt, powered by the wisdom of the market: it routes based on what the OpenRouter community collectively spends on for exactly the kind of task your prompt represents, looking at spend over a trailing 7-day window. Openrouter says the router considers factors like task type, model capabilities, tool support, and cost. The Auto Router was released on November 8, 2023.",
            "The family has two slugs. Auto (openrouter/auto) works like any other model slug, and Auto Beta (openrouter/auto-beta) is the early-access track where new routing behaviors land before they reach openrouter/auto. Openrouter says Auto Beta is the experimental version where new improvements are tested, and that when new improvements are proven in auto-beta, they graduate to the auto router. Auto Router (Beta) was released on July 17, 2026. Each slug only reads settings sent under its own plugin id, auto-router or auto-beta-router.",
            "Openrouter offers these models through its API, which is OpenAI-compatible, so most SDKs work by swapping the base URL. Openrouter says Auto Router has no fixed price of its own: each request is billed at the price of the model that serves it. The cost_tier setting (low, medium, high, xhigh, or max) selects how much you are willing to pay, and the default is low. Auto Router can route to models with context windows of up to 2,000,000 tokens, and it accepts text, images, audio, files such as PDFs, and video as input and returns text and images."
        ],
        "written_on": "2026-10-07"
